# Guardrails
- Use targeted replace_in_file edits; never rewrite a >400-line file whole.
- Read narrowly: grep/search_codebase to locate a symbol first, then read only
  that +-30 line window. Never whole-read a large file when a range will do.
- Confirm edits with `git diff --stat` / `git diff <file>` instead of re-reading.
- Pipe verification output through `tail -n 40` / `grep`; only dump full logs on failure.
- Batch independent reads/searches/edits into one tool call.

# Workflow
- Plan mode: explore the minimum, record a TASK.md with `- [ ]` boxes, file paths,
  one-line Potential Bugs, and a concrete Verification Step. Present plan, then wait.
- Act mode: read TASK.md's ACTIVE phase only; execute unchecked items in order;
  mark `- [x]` only after the Verification Step passes.

# Database (standing instruction from user)
- ALWAYS author DB changes as an idempotent timestamped migration under
  `supabase/migrations/`, then APPLY IT YOURSELF with
  `npx supabase db push --yes < /dev/null`. Never leave a migration unapplied and
  never ask the user to run it by hand — they are already logged in + linked.
- Then VERIFY against the live DB (read-only query) before reporting done.
- `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` cannot rename a column (42P16): `drop view if exists`
  first, then `create view` (matches `src/services/schema.sql`).
- One-time data fixes are migrations too, guarded so they are no-ops on re-run
  (e.g. `where id = '…' and river_name is null`).

# Terminal safety
- NEVER run the same failing command more than twice consecutively; then STOP and
  summarize the error + ask for guidance.
- No blocking foreground servers in the tool window (background + redirect to /tmp).

# Memory
- Append a concise 1-2 line entry to CHANGELOG_INTERNAL.md at each feature/phase end.
- New chat: read only the last ~20 lines of CHANGELOG_INTERNAL.md + the active
  TASK.md phase (not full history).

# Continuous improvement
- On a style/architecture/tool correction: ask to persist it to .clinerules.
